> The variables x and y seem to not be well-defined. They represent the data
> values in some cases, but are also sometimes used for geometric properties, in
> ways that aren't always consistent with the data. For example, x initially means
> the x position of the data; but after pos_dodge, it's modified to the value
> (xmin+xmax)/2, which is the center of the of the geometric object. If the
> meaning of x is supposed to change, it would be helpful to have definitions
> like, "at stage A, x means this, and at stage B, x means that." Or if the data x
> is different from the geom's x, perhaps there should be two different variables.
