My idea is like this:

df <- data.frame(x = 1:3, y = 1:3, colour = 1:3, label = letters[1:3])
ggplot(df, aes_auto())
# define x, y, colour, label

df <- data.frame(xp = 1:3, y = 1:3, colour = 1:3, txt = letters[1:3], foo = 1:3)
ggplot(df, aes_auto(x = xp, label = txt))
# define xp as x, y, colour, txt as label, and drop foo.

Technically, it would be possible, if aes_auto() can access the data.

Or, simply,

aes_auto(x = x, ..., data = df)

might be better (but there may be overhead for copy of df, if df is large data).

